Usage: xfmodel [Options] input_file output_file
Options can be abbreviated, current short name abbreviations are in parentheses
Options:
 -input (-in)  OR  -InputFile   File
    Input model file
 -output (-o)  OR  -OutputFile   File
    Output file, either transformed model or list of transformations.
 -image (-im)  OR  -ImageFile   File
    Image file that model was built on (optional)
 -piece (-pi)  OR  -PieceListFile   File
    Name of piece list file for a montaged image file
 -allz (-al)  OR  -AllZhaveTransforms
    All Z values have transforms in even though the image has gaps in Z
 -center (-ce)  OR  -CenterInXandY   2 floats
    Center coordinates of image in X and Y (optional)
 -transonly (-t)  OR  -TranslationOnly
    Solve only for translations in X and Y
 -rottrans (-r)  OR  -RotationTranslation
    Solve for rotations and translations
 -magrot (-m)  OR  -MagRotTrans
    Solve for magnifications, rotations, and translations
 -sections (-se)  OR  -SectionsToAnalyze   List
    Sections to find transformations for (numbered from 0)
 -single (-si)  OR  -SingleSection   Int
    Align all sections to the given section
 -full (-f)  OR  -FullReportMeanAndMax   2 floats
    Criterion mean deviation and maximum deviation for full report on a
    section
 -prealign (-pr)  OR  -PrealignTransforms   File
    File of g transforms used to prealign the images modeled
 -edit (-e)  OR  -EditTransforms   File
    File with existing transforms to be replaced by any transforms found
 -xforms (-x)  OR  -XformsToApply   File
    Transforms to apply to the model
 -useline (-use)  OR  -UseTransformLine   Int
    Line number of single transform to apply to whole model (numbered from 0)
 -chunks (-ch)  OR  -ChunkSizes   List
    Size of chunk of sections corresponding to each transform in file
 -back (-ba)  OR  -BackTransform
    Back-transform or re-distort model
 -scale (-sc)  OR  -ScaleShifts   Float
    Factor to scale X/Y translations before applying transforms factors
 -adjust (-ad)  OR  -AdjustForRotationBy90   Int
    Adjust for 90-degree rotation: 1 to do if detected, 2 to do regardless
 -distort (-d)  OR  -DistortionField   File
    Undistort/redistort model with image distortion field in this file
 -binning (-bi)  OR  -BinningOfImages   Float
    The camera binning at which images were taken
 -gradient (-g)  OR  -GradientFile   File
    File with magnification gradients to be applied for each Z value
 -param (-pa)  OR  -ParameterFile   File
    Read parameter entries from file
 -help (-h)  OR  -usage
    Print help output
